    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Summary",
      "html": "<p>This optional unit adds 50 words that occur 10 times in the New Testament and are not in Machen&#x27;s lessons: 19 nouns, 20 verbs and 11 other words. Nothing in the course waits for them; they are here so that you can read the New Testament with the lexicon open less often. Learn them on the Words track: recognize, recall, type, type with accents.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Built from words you know",
      "html": "<p>These verbs are a preposition plus a verb from the lessons; the meaning usually follows from the parts: ἐκπίπτω (πίπτω); παράγω (ἄγω).</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Common confusion",
      "html": "<p>Look-alikes that differ by one letter: ἀφαιρέω (I take away) and ἀναιρέω (I take up); βίος (life) and υἱός (a son); ἰσχύς (strength) and ἰσχύω (I am strong); κλητός (called) and κλῆρος (a lot); κομίζω (I bring) and νομίζω (I think); ὄντως (really) and οὕτως (thus); ὅρκος (an oath) and οἶκος (a house). Feminine although they end in -ος, like ὁδός: βίβλος, κοινωνός.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Source",
      "html": "<p>Words chosen by their New Testament frequency (MorphGNT); glosses after Jeffrey Dodson&#x27;s Greek-English lexicon (public domain).</p>"
    },
